/*!
\page page_stTpcHitCollection StTpcHitCollection

\ref StTpcHitCollection is the top-level container for all reconstructed hits in the STAR Time
Projection Chamber (TPC). Hits are stored in a three-level hierarchy — <b>sector → padrow → hit</b>
— mirroring the physical readout geometry of the TPC. The two supporting classes,
\ref StTpcSectorHitCollection and \ref StTpcPadrowHitCollection, are internal nodes of that
hierarchy and are not used independently.

\section sec_tpc_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\verbatim
StTpcHitCollection          (top level, 24 sectors)
└── StTpcSectorHitCollection    (one per sector, up to 100 padrows)
    └── StTpcPadrowHitCollection    (one per padrow, holds StTpcHit* pointers)
\endverbatim

All three classes inherit from StObject.

\section sec_tpc_containment Containment Model

- \ref StTpcHitCollection holds an embedded array of 24 \ref StTpcSectorHitCollection objects
  (<tt>mSectors[24]</tt>).
- Each \ref StTpcSectorHitCollection holds an embedded array of up to 100
  \ref StTpcPadrowHitCollection objects (<tt>mPadrows[100]</tt>).
- Each \ref StTpcPadrowHitCollection holds a dynamic <tt>StSPtrVecTpcHit mHits</tt> vector of
  pointers to \ref StTpcHit objects.

\ref StTpcHitCollection::addHit "addHit(StTpcHit*)" routes an \ref StTpcHit into the correct
<tt>mHits</tt> vector using the hit's own 1-based <tt>sector()</tt> and <tt>padrow()</tt>
accessors, converting internally to 0-based array indices. The public accessor methods
<tt>sector()</tt> and <tt>padrow()</tt> use <b>0-based</b> indices.

\section sec_tpc_ownership Object Ownership

\subsection subsec_tpc_subcoll Sub-collection Storage
\ref StTpcSectorHitCollection and \ref StTpcPadrowHitCollection objects are
<b>stack-allocated as plain arrays</b> inside their parent. They are not heap-allocated and must
not be deleted by the caller.

\subsection subsec_tpc_hits Hit Storage — StSPtrVecTpcHit
The per-padrow hit vector is of type <tt>StSPtrVecTpcHit</tt>, a <em>smart-pointer vector</em>.
\ref StTpcPadrowHitCollection::~StTpcPadrowHitCollection "~StTpcPadrowHitCollection()" iterates
over the vector and explicitly <tt>delete</tt>s each <tt>StTpcHit*</tt>. This explicit deletion is
required because \ref StTpcHit uses a custom <tt>new</tt>/<tt>delete</tt> via
<tt>StMemoryPool</tt>.

\warning Do <b>not</b> <tt>delete</tt> \ref StTpcHit pointers obtained from the collection.
Ownership belongs to \ref StTpcPadrowHitCollection; external deletion will cause a double-free.

\subsection subsec_tpc_framework Framework Ownership
\ref StTpcHitCollection itself is owned by the StEvent framework (via the
<tt>St_DataSet</tt>/<tt>StXRefMain</tt> mechanism). When registered with StEvent via
<tt>StEvent::setTpcHitCollection()</tt>, ownership transfers to the framework, which handles
cleanup. <tt>StTpcHitCollection::~StTpcHitCollection()</tt> is a no-op.

\section sec_tpc_members Data Members

\subsection subsec_tpc_members_top StTpcHitCollection
- <tt>enum { mNumberOfSectors = 24 }</tt> — Fixed number of TPC readout sectors.
- <tt>StTpcSectorHitCollection mSectors[24]</tt> — Embedded array of per-sector collections.

\subsection subsec_tpc_members_sector StTpcSectorHitCollection
- <tt>enum { mNumberOfPadrows = 100 }</tt> — Maximum number of padrows per sector.
- <tt>StTpcPadrowHitCollection mPadrows[100]</tt> — Embedded array of per-padrow collections.

\subsection subsec_tpc_members_padrow StTpcPadrowHitCollection
- <tt>StSPtrVecTpcHit mHits</tt> — Dynamic vector of pointers to \ref StTpcHit objects in this
  padrow.

\section sec_tpc_methods Key Methods

\subsection subsec_tpc_methods_top StTpcHitCollection
- <tt>bool addHit(StTpcHit*)</tt> — Routes a hit into the correct sector/padrow sub-collection.
  Returns <tt>false</tt> if the hit is null or its indices are out of range.
- <tt>unsigned int numberOfHits() const</tt> — Total hits across all sectors and padrows.
- <tt>unsigned int numberOfSectors() const</tt> — Returns 24.
- <tt>unsigned int numberOfPadrows(int sectorId) const</tt> — Padrow count for the given 0-based
  sector index.
- <tt>StTpcSectorHitCollection* sector(unsigned int)</tt> — Returns the sub-collection at the
  given 0-based index, or <tt>nullptr</tt> if out of range.
- <tt>const StSPtrVecTpcHit* hits(int sectorId, int padrowId) const</tt> — Returns the hit vector
  for the given 0-based sector and padrow, or <tt>nullptr</tt> if out of range.
- <tt>StTpcHitIter begin() / end()</tt> — Forward iterators over all hits in the collection.

\subsection subsec_tpc_methods_sector StTpcSectorHitCollection
- <tt>unsigned int numberOfHits() const</tt> — Total hits in this sector.
- <tt>unsigned int numberOfPadrows() const</tt> — Returns 100.
- <tt>StTpcPadrowHitCollection* padrow(unsigned int)</tt> — Sub-collection at 0-based index.

\subsection subsec_tpc_methods_padrow StTpcPadrowHitCollection
- <tt>StSPtrVecTpcHit& hits()</tt> — Mutable reference to the hit vector.
- <tt>const StSPtrVecTpcHit& hits() const</tt> — Const reference to the hit vector.

\subsection subsec_tpc_methods_iter StTpcHitCollection::StTpcHitIter (inner class)
An <tt>std::input_iterator</tt>-compatible iterator that traverses all hits, automatically skipping
empty padrows and sectors.
- <tt>static StTpcHitIter begin(StTpcHitCollection&)</tt>
- <tt>static StTpcHitIter end(StTpcHitCollection&)</tt>
- <tt>StTpcHitIter& operator++()</tt>
- <tt>const StTpcHit* operator*() const</tt>

\section sec_tpc_usage Usage Examples

\subsection subsec_tpc_usage_iter Iterate Using the Built-in Iterator (recommended)

\code{.cpp}
StTpcHitCollection* tpcColl = event->tpcHitCollection();
if (tpcColl) {
    for (const StTpcHit* hit : *tpcColl) {  // range-for via begin()/end()
        // process hit
    }
}
\endcode

\subsection subsec_tpc_usage_nested Iterate by Sector and Padrow (explicit nested loops)

\code{.cpp}
StTpcHitCollection* tpcColl = event->tpcHitCollection();
if (!tpcColl) return;

for (unsigned int iSec = 0; iSec < tpcColl->numberOfSectors(); ++iSec) {
    const StTpcSectorHitCollection* sec = tpcColl->sector(iSec);
    if (!sec) continue;

    for (unsigned int iRow = 0; iRow < sec->numberOfPadrows(); ++iRow) {
        const StTpcPadrowHitCollection* row = sec->padrow(iRow);
        if (!row) continue;

        const StSPtrVecTpcHit& hits = row->hits();
        for (const StTpcHit* hit : hits) {
            // process hit -- do NOT delete hit
        }
    }
}
\endcode

\subsection subsec_tpc_usage_add Add a Hit (e.g. from a Maker)

\code{.cpp}
StTpcHit* hit = new StTpcHit(/*...*/);  // allocated via StTpcHit::operator new
tpcColl->addHit(hit);                   // ownership transferred to the collection
// Do not delete 'hit' after this call.
\endcode

*/
